  "id": "agentic-state",
  "term": "agentic state",
  "definition": "Agentic state is a proposed condition used to explain obedience in which, when faced with an authority figure, a person focuses on that authority’s demands and becomes less responsive to the suffering of the person affected by their actions. In the packet, this idea is presented as a traditional explanation of behavior in Milgram’s obedience studies.",
